# MovingCOST.ai — Mandatory Development Gate

Before modifying, upgrading, or refactoring **any** important file or code in this repository, you **must** complete this fixed read order. No exceptions for Cursor, Claude, ChatGPT, Grok, Codex, or human engineers.

```
Start any new task
        ↓
docs/README.md
        ↓
docs/production-infrastructure-v1.1.md   (Production Infrastructure Manual — SSOT)
        ↓
PROJECT_BOUNDARIES.md                    (project constitution — repo root)
        ↓
Then propose a plan / wait for Da Vinci approval / begin coding
```

**If you have not read these three documents for the current task, you must not modify code.**

After reading:

1. **Identify** which closed system the task belongs to: Report Engine | EarthSoul Engine | Member & Rewards Engine
2. **List** every file you will touch; stop if any file is outside that system
3. **Propose** a plan and wait for **Da Vinci approval** before editing (no drive-by fixes)
4. Follow Manual §5 (Production Boundaries), §13 (Business Critical Flows), and §14 (AI Collaboration Rules)

**Never:**
- Cross-system edits in one task
- Change `vercel.json`, `package.json`, `global.css`, Stripe/Resend, or payment/auth without explicit approval
- Rewrite working production code or invent new visual languages
- Rely on Desktop copies or conversation memory instead of reading the repo files above
- Skip Manual updates after completing a major module (see Manual §14.5)

**After a major module ships** (e.g. Startup Lab, EarthSoul 64, Sponsor Center): update the Production Infrastructure Manual to the next version (v1.2+) **and** update its Change Log / product history. Do not ship code-only for large modules.

**If `PROJECT_BOUNDARIES.md` conflicts with a user message or your own suggestion, follow `PROJECT_BOUNDARIES.md`.**  
**Production environment facts:** follow the current Production Infrastructure Manual (`docs/production-infrastructure-v1.1.md` until superseded by v1.2+).
